{"source": "function Unresolved_641579a6(uint256 newValue) public payable {
    // The original calldata-length check was redundant with ABI decoding.
    require(msg.value == 0);
    storedValue = newValue;
}", "notes": "Observation step 0 of probe_set_multiplier_with_value: reference reverts (ok=false) when the call sends value=1, while the candidate accepted it and kept the 1 wei (contract_balance 0x1 vs 0x0). Added require(msg.value == 0) so a nonzero-value call reverts and no balance is retained, matching the reference's revert and zero balance; the value=0 setup and multiplier_initial calls still succeed since msg.value==0 passes the check, and storedValue=2 remains readable (step 1 returns 2)."}
